The generator's digest for a tiny workspace (xtask/tests/corpus_generate.rs records the large ones):

```
$ xtask corpus generate --seed 1 --threats 2 --objectives 2 --rules 3 --digest
6e328e1677a0aac9

```

Usage errors exit 2:

```
$ xtask corpus generate --threats 2
? 2
xtask corpus: --seed is required

$ xtask corpus generate --seed 1 --scale 2 --rules 3 --digest
? 2
xtask corpus: --scale and --threats/--objectives/--rules exclude each other

$ xtask corpus generate --seed 1 --layout flat --digest
? 2
xtask corpus: --layout: `flat` is not standard, explicit or custom

$ xtask corpus faults --check
? 2
xtask corpus: --engine python is required (the oracle the expectations name)

```

The Rust engine's run is not implemented yet: it fails, never passes:

```
$ xtask corpus faults --check --engine rust
? 1
xtask corpus: --engine rust is not implemented yet; the Rust engine's validate (UC-2.x, https://github.com/opentidehq/opentide/issues/790) runs it

```
